From 1c7a0fe470b41f28dcdab15f7a2aeb56b3511d12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Brum?= <andre.brum@softlive.com.br>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:46:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ppu_lifter: arbitrate the jump-table base register by
 validated targets

`discover_jump_tables` picks the `lwzx` operand holding the table base by taking
the FIRST candidate whose nearest definition is a base load, then breaks out of
the loop. The `add`-based reordering just above only moves a candidate to the
front when an `add` combines the loaded value with it -- which is the OFFSET
table idiom. On an ABSOLUTE table there is no such `add`, so the order stays the
raw lwzx operand order.

That is enough to lose whole dispatchers. When the index operand also carries a
TOC load -- the stale `lwz idx,d(r2)` bleeding in from the preceding function
through the 30-instruction window, exactly the collision the comment in this
function already describes -- the index wins, the wrong table base is read, no
entry validates, `best` stays empty, and the dispatcher is dropped silently.

Fix: apply the principle this function already uses for multi-TOC executables --
do not guess which candidate is right, try each and keep the one that validates
the most targets -- to the base-register candidate as well. Collect every
operand that resolves to a base, then run the existing decode loop once per
(base, toc) pair and keep the best. Ties go to the earlier candidate, which is
the `add`-paired one whenever the reordering fired, so the syntactic preference
survives as a cheap tie-break instead of being the final decision.

Everything else is preserved and simply moves inside the per-candidate loop
unchanged: the two-level base walk with its blr-bounded widening, the 64-bit
`sldi;add;lwz` idiom synthesis, `_read_ptr`'s ELFv1 high-word check, the
largest-immediate case count matched against the raw index, and the generous
`scan` with structural end-of-table termination.

tools/test_ppu_jumptables.py is new: eight hand-assembled vectors, no SDK, no
ELF, no network. Seven of them decode identically before and after this commit;
the eighth (absolute table, both lwzx operands TOC-loaded, wrong one first) goes
from a dropped dispatcher to three resolved case targets. The linux workflow
already globs tools/test_*.py under `set -e`, so it runs with no CI change.

  vector                                     before   after
  one-level absolute                         3        3
  two-level indirection                      2        2
  offset table                               2        2
  multi-TOC                                  2        2
  offset + first-operand collision           2        2
  ABSOLUTE + first-operand collision         dropped  3
  scalar toc / toc=None                      ok       ok

test_ppu_lift.py, test_ppu_branches.py and test_lifter_dedupe.py pass unchanged.
lift_selftest.py was not exercised: it needs the PS3 SDK PPU compiler.

Evidence level: offline-unit. Nothing here was measured in-boot.
